step_details.raw_response:
Thought: Start with a simple robust baseline – mean over the full model pool.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"mean","pool":"pool_full"}

Thought: Evaluate a weighted combination using inverse error to see if it improves on the mean baseline.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: Test the best single model (catboost) to see if a single strong model beats the robust mean baseline.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"best_single","model":"catboost"}

Thought: Test a robust median combination over the full model pool to see if it beats the best single catboost.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"median","pool":"pool_full"}

Thought: Test a weighted combo using the pooled_meta_model handle (w1) over the full pool to see if a learned weighting beats the best single catboost.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"w1"}

Thought: Test a trimmed‑mean combination over the full pool to see if trimming the extremes improves the robust mean baseline.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"trimmed_mean","pool":"pool_full","trim_pct":0.2}

Thought: Test whether a different single model (rf) outperforms catboost as the best single.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"best_single","model":"rf"}

Thought: Test a dynamic Bayesian averaging (dba) over the full model pool to see if it can outperform the best single catboost.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"dba","pool":"pool_full","dba_max_iter":30}

Thought: Test a weighted combination using inverse_error on a smaller, correlated-error pool (pool1) to see if focusing on a subset improves over the full‑pool weighted baseline.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool1","weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: Test a weighted combination on a slightly different pool (pool2) to see if removing some correlated models improves performance.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool2","weights":"inverse_error"}

Thought: Test a trimmed‑mean combination on the smaller, more stable pool1 to see if trimming extremes improves over the current best single.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"trimmed_mean","pool":"pool1","trim_pct":0.2}

Thought: Test a simple mean combination over the smaller, more stable pool1 to see if a reduced robust average improves over the best single.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"mean","pool":"pool1"}

